ire the most legendary  loot the battle between Heaven and Hell  rages on when Diablo 4 Launches on all  systems on 6 6 2023  two of the biggest titles in the Persona  series are finally getting revitalized  for modern consoles Persona 3 Portable  and Persona 4 Golden although Persona 4  Golden has been released more widely on  Steam recently this is the first time  Persona 3 Portable will be playable  outside of its PSP and Vita releases if  you've played Persona 5 you'll be  familiar with the moment-to-moment  gameplay of Persona 3 and 4. develop  your Social Links and interact with the  day-to-day activities of your school  while also entering Twisted Dungeons and  otherworldly Dimensions to fight  monsters Persona 3 Portable also has  dual protagonists the only time this has  ever been a feature in the series  allowing you to choose a male or female  option for your main character that will  affect how you move through your  day-to-day both games launch on all  systems on January 18th 2023  Final Fantasy VII rebirth continues the  heralded tale of cloud and Company from  Final Fantasy VII remake and will cover  the middle chapter of the Final Fantasy  VII story not much is known about the  project but game director tetsuya namura  has stated that development is  progressing rapidly in the final entry  in the trilogy is already in development  rebirth is expected on Playstation  between winter 2023 to early 2024.  the next installment in the storied  series final fantasy 16 features  fast-paced magic and swordplay with a  combat system developed by Devil May Cry  and Dragon's Dogma veteran ryota Suzuki  the story follows the life of Clive  rossfield the son of an Archduke spread  across the different seasons of his life  and the ever-changing political dramas  and conflicts between his and other  kingdoms throughout the realm in  contrast to Final Fantasy XV the world  is not open to explore but will feature  large explorable areas throughout the  linear progress